<h1>JamVerse — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: 20 October 2026</p>

<p>JamVerse ("the app") is developed by João Gonçalves (BackingTracksVerse), Portugal. This policy explains what happens to your information when you use the app.</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p><strong>JamVerse does not collect, store on our servers, sell or share any personal data.</strong> The app has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no tracking.</p>

<h2>Microphone and audio</h2>
<p>The app uses the microphone / audio input only to process your guitar signal in real time (amp, cab and effects) and for the tuner. Audio is processed entirely on your device. It is never recorded, saved or sent anywhere.</p>

<h2>Files you load</h2>
<p>NAM captures and IR files that you choose to load are copied into the app's private storage on your device so they are available next time. They are never uploaded.</p>

<h2>Settings and presets</h2>
<p>Your presets, saved progressions, language and session are stored only on your device. Deleting the app removes them.</p>

<h2>Purchases</h2>
<p>Subscriptions and purchases are processed by Apple through the App Store. We do not receive or store your payment details. Apple's privacy policy applies to these transactions: <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">apple.com/legal/privacy</a>.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The app does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with a new date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions: <a href="mailto:info@backingtracksverse.com">info@backingtracksverse.com</a> · <a href="https://backingtracksverse.com">backingtracksverse.com</a></p>
</section>

